PATCH 131: render the ABOUT dialog credit TEXT + OK button (bit-identical to DOSBox) and fix the wasm
dialog-path OOB.  Completes the ABOUT sub-screen (panel from patch 129/130 -> full credits + OK button).

Root cause of the missing credits: the ABOUT dialog's paint methods for the credit-text element (nd=d4)
and the button elements (nd=d6) are `lcall [id*2 - 0x739f]` / `lcall [id*2 - 0x7393]` -- FAR calls
through the per-dialog method table (offset:seg word pairs).  For ABOUT (id=4) they dispatch to
0f69:0x7606 = FUN_1000_6c96 (the credit-TEXT drawer: title + 3 credit columns + copyright, drawn via
52d1 setpos / 5591 multi-line drawstring with the 0x0c/0x0e line-format control chars) and 0f69:0x76ad
= FUN_1000_6d3d (the OK-button sprite draw).  Patch 129 rendered both as NEAR calls to the wrong seg-0
offsets, so neither drew.  Restore the faithful FAR dispatch and thread the per-element register args.

- 71f8 (nd=d4 credit-text paint method): FAR dispatch -> FUN_1000_6c96.
- 7203 (nd=d6 button paint method): si=[bx+2]; ax=[bp+si+1] (button state); bx+=4; FAR dispatch ->
  FUN_1000_6d3d(state, rect).  bx = current element (209e stored DGROUP:0x3e08); bp = base (fafe).
- FUN_1000_6d3d: reconstruct the button sprite draw (per-state sprite table [state*2-0x7387] + [0x8be9]
  sprite base; lcall [0x6b4] = MGAVIDEO 26a1 sprite blit with ax=sprite, bx=rect).  Ghidra base-loss.
- e39f: thread the dropped SAVE/RESTORE-blit args (dx=save-descriptor 0xf6ee, bx=rect DAT_2000_b6f2) to
  the [0x602] far call.  This is the WASM-OOB ROOT CAUSE: the dropped args ran 0fbc/0fe4 on garbage --
  harmless on native (di_save garbage 0x0004, flag byte 0 -> early return) but on wasm the garbage was
  0/0 (flag 0xa0 -> a bogus save_seg->fb copy) which wasm's bounds check trapped as "memory access out
  of bounds".  Threading the args faithfully makes 0fe4 take its real early-return on both targets ->
  native<->wasm identical, no OOB.
